1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,040
Look at your television.

2
00:00:02,040 --> 00:00:03,840
It's a sheet of glass.

3
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:06,520
Flat, cold, a bit dusty.

4
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:08,440
And yet a whole world is living

5
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:11,900
inside it: a storm, a goal, someone's

6
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:14,300
face crying at exactly the right moment.

7
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:17,640
So where is the picture coming from?

8
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:18,740
Not the glass.

9
00:00:18,740 --> 00:00:19,700
I checked.

10
00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:21,820
Let's unscrew the back and follow it.

11
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:25,540
Warning: this involves a screwdriver and mild

12
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:26,420
guilt.

13
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:28,940
Do this on your grandfather's set and

14
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:30,800
you find something absurd.

15
00:00:30,980 --> 00:00:33,220
A glass bottle, nearly all the air

16
00:00:33,220 --> 00:00:34,440
sucked out.

17
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:35,960
And at the far end of it,

18
00:00:35,960 --> 00:00:36,920
a gun.

19
00:00:37,260 --> 00:00:40,540
It fires electrons, billions a second, at

20
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:41,480
the back of the screen.

21
00:00:42,220 --> 00:00:44,120
The glass is coated in dust that

22
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:45,720
glows when it's hit.

23
00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:47,380
One dot of light.

24
00:00:47,440 --> 00:00:49,540
But one dot is not a picture.

25
00:00:50,020 --> 00:00:52,600
So magnets sweep the beam, left to

26
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:56,220
right, line after line, the whole screen,

27
00:00:56,220 --> 00:00:57,740
sixty times every second.

28
00:00:58,480 --> 00:01:00,440
Your heart can't manage that.

29
00:01:00,440 --> 00:01:02,120
Your television does it all evening.

30
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:04,420
Too fast for your eye.

31
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:05,820
You don't see a dot.

32
00:01:05,780 --> 00:01:07,160
You see a face.

33
00:01:07,480 --> 00:01:09,180
Colour is a cheat.

34
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:12,520
Three kinds of glowing dust, red, green

35
00:01:12,520 --> 00:01:14,840
and blue, in dots too small to

36
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:15,540
see.

37
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:17,860
A metal sieve makes sure each beam

38
00:01:17,860 --> 00:01:20,500
only hits its own colour.

39
00:01:19,520 --> 00:01:21,860
Mix them, and your brain does the

40
00:01:21,860 --> 00:01:22,500
rest.

41
00:01:22,920 --> 00:01:24,300
Put a drop of water on an

42
00:01:24,300 --> 00:01:27,000
old screen and you'll spot them: tiny

43
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:28,500
stripes of colour.

44
00:01:28,680 --> 00:01:30,160
Everyone thinks that's the picture.

45
00:01:30,780 --> 00:01:31,780
It's only the ingredients.

46
00:01:32,780 --> 00:01:34,140
That was the old way.

47
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:37,480
Glass, vacuum, a gun.

48
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:39,960
Heavy, hot, and a nightmare to carry

49
00:01:39,960 --> 00:01:40,980
upstairs.

50
00:01:41,360 --> 00:01:43,700
The flat ones threw the gun away.

51
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:45,320
Instead, a sandwich.

52
00:01:45,140 --> 00:01:47,300
A lamp at the back.

53
00:01:46,740 --> 00:01:48,400
A filter.

54
00:01:47,860 --> 00:01:50,400
A liquid that twists light like a

55
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:51,240
turnstile.

56
00:01:50,980 --> 00:01:52,920
A second filter.

57
00:01:52,420 --> 00:01:55,440
Twist it one way, light gets through.

58
00:01:54,940 --> 00:01:57,320
The other way, it's blocked.

59
00:01:57,340 --> 00:02:00,280
Millions of tiny turnstiles, each with its

60
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:01,600
own colour.

61
00:02:01,780 --> 00:02:03,800
OLED went one better.

62
00:02:03,780 --> 00:02:04,760
No lamp.

63
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:07,460
Every pixel makes its own light, so

64
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:10,300
when it switches off, it's truly black.

65
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:11,680
Not dark grey.

66
00:02:11,680 --> 00:02:12,240
Black.

67
00:02:12,940 --> 00:02:14,020
But wait.

68
00:02:14,020 --> 00:02:15,840
Nobody ran a wire from the storm

69
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:17,100
to your wall.

70
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:19,460
The picture arrived through the air.

71
00:02:19,540 --> 00:02:21,320
A metal stick on a roof catches

72
00:02:21,320 --> 00:02:21,600
it.

73
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:24,500
The tower shouts the whole picture as

74
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:24,840
ripples.

75
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:27,440
Back then it was shouted as raw

76
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:28,460
waves.

77
00:02:28,580 --> 00:02:31,000
Now it's mostly numbers, but the idea

78
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,900
is the same: ripples in, light out.

79
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:36,280
A chip in your set catches them,

80
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:39,080
and untangles the picture from the sound.

81
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:41,200
So here's the trick.

82
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:42,460
Ripples in the air.

83
00:02:42,460 --> 00:02:45,440
A beam, or a twisting liquid, or

84
00:02:45,440 --> 00:02:47,020
a glowing pixel.

85
00:02:46,380 --> 00:02:49,260
Three colours too small to see.

86
00:02:49,260 --> 00:02:52,480
And your brain, filling in the rest.

87
00:02:52,360 --> 00:02:54,260
The world in the glass was never

88
00:02:54,260 --> 00:02:55,800
in the glass.

89
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:57,160
It was always in you.

